# Talk about a traveller standing nearby (doc 30, topic player). {subject} is the traveller's name when the speaker
# knows them (known=yes), or how they look when not (known=no: "a grey she-wolf"), so a stranger's description sits
# mid-sentence. Speak of the traveller as "they". Alternatives are written in parallel.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Strangers: curious

scene ev_pl_new_face
when topic=player topic.known=no
a : See #topic.subject# over there? Never seen them before. | Who's that? Look at #topic.subject#, fresh off the road. | There's #topic.subject# watching the street.
b[guard] : I've had my eye on them since the gate.
b[child] : Are they an adventurer? Do they have a sword?
b : New face. | Travellers come and go. | Let them watch.
a : Wonder what brings them. | They do. Mostly go. | Watching what, though?

scene ev_pl_road_dust
when topic=player topic.known=no
a : Look at the road dust on #topic.subject#. Come a long way. | Smell #topic.subject# by the wall? Somewhere far off. | Sniff the air near #topic.subject#. Pine and river, I'd say.
b[carter] : That's west-road dust. Red. I'd know it anywhere.
b : Long way, by the paws on them. | Far off, and tired. | Good nose.
a : Long road, then. | Tired and hungry, I'd guess. | Best in the street.

scene ev_pl_coat
when topic=player topic.known=no
a : Fine coat on #topic.subject#, isn't it? | Have you ever seen markings like #topic.subject# has? | Look at #topic.subject#. Odd colouring for these parts.
b[noble] : Common enough, in the south. One sees it at court.
b[old] : My grandsire had markings like that. Southern blood.
b : Very handsome. | Never. | Odd, but fine.
a : I'd have a coat like that. | Striking. | Fine, yes.

scene ev_pl_wondering_job
when topic=player topic.known=no
a : What do you think #topic.subject# does for a living? | See how #topic.subject# stands? Like a soldier. | Bet you #topic.subject# is a merchant. Look at those eyes.
b[merchant] : Not a merchant. Merchants look at stalls, not faces.
b : Hard to say. | Could be. | Merchant? Maybe a thief.
a : Something with walking. | Or used to. | Same eyes, some would say.

scene ev_pl_newcomer_hope
when topic=player topic.known=no here.place=tavern
a : Look, #topic.subject# just came in. Buy them a drink? | Think #topic.subject# has news from the road? | I'd say #topic.subject# could use a seat by the fire.
b[innkeeper] : Strangers drink like everyone else. I'll see to it.
b : You buy it. | Ask them. | Move over, then.
a : I might. | I will, once they've eaten. | I'm moving.

scene ev_pl_child_staring
when topic=player topic.known=no a.stage=young|adolescent
a : Look! Look at #topic.subject#! | Mama, who's #topic.subject#? | Do you think #topic.subject# has been to the sea?
b[old] : It's rude to point, pup.
b : Don't stare, it's rude. | A traveller. | Maybe. Ask politely.
a : I'm not staring, I'm looking! | Can I go talk to them? | I'm too shy.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Strangers: wary

scene ev_pl_suspicious
when topic=player topic.known=no
a : I don't like the look of #topic.subject#. | I've seen #topic.subject# hanging about the stalls all morning. | Keep an eye on #topic.subject#. Shifty.
b[guard] : Noted. If they're trouble, they'll learn fast.
b[merchant] : Then I'll keep my paw on the coin box.
b : You don't like anyone. | Looking, maybe. | You think everyone's shifty.
a : I've good reasons. | Looking, or counting. | Usually right, though.

scene ev_pl_suspicious_night
when topic=player topic.known=no here.time=dusk|night
a : Who's #topic.subject#, out at this hour? | I've watched #topic.subject# in the shadows a while now. | Strange time for a stranger to be wandering.
b[guard] : I'll have a word, if they're still here at the next bell.
b : Lost, maybe. | Let them be. | Strange, yes.
a : Or not lost at all. | Let's go inside. | Bar the door tonight.

scene ev_pl_ser_ferro_judge
when topic=player topic.known=no here.region=ridgemere
a : I'd say #topic.subject# isn't a Ridgemere wolf. | Do you think #topic.subject# has a permit from the City Office? | Somebody should tell #topic.subject# to bathe before the Heights.
b[official] : Every visitor is noted at the gate. In principle.
b : Countryside, by the walk. | The Watch will ask. | Hush, they'll hear.
a : Country wolves. Always staring at the walls. | They always do. | Let them.

scene ev_pl_ridgemere_judge
when topic=player topic.known=no here.region=rain_coast
a : Look at #topic.subject#. Not dressed for our rain. | Look, #topic.subject# has stopped to stare at the Sound. | Whoever #topic.subject# is, they're not from Ridgemere. Too dry.
b[fisher] : Two days here and they'll have webbed paws.
b : They'll learn. | First sight of the Sound, maybe. | Not for long.
a : Soon enough. | It takes you, the first time. | Give it a day.

scene ev_pl_fortress
when topic=player topic.known=no here.place=barracks
a : A civilian in the barracks, #topic.subject#. Odd. | Who let #topic.subject# in? | I hope #topic.subject# has business here.
b[guard] : Business with the captain, I heard. Keep your mouth shut.
b : Messenger, maybe. | The door watch, obviously. | They will, or they won't stay.
a : Messengers carry pouches. | Then they'd better be right. | Ha. True.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Strangers: admiring or rude

scene ev_pl_handsome
when topic=player topic.known=no a.stage=adult|adolescent
a : Have you seen #topic.subject#? Very handsome. | Did you see the eyes on #topic.subject#? Brightest I've ever seen. | I think #topic.subject# smiled at me.
b[spouses] : I'm standing right here, you know.
b : Go and say something. | Eyes like amber. | Smiled? Or bared their teeth?
a : I couldn't. | Amber, exactly. | A smile. Definitely a smile.

scene ev_pl_rude
when topic=player topic.known=no
a : Somebody should point #topic.subject# to the bathhouse. | Who does #topic.subject# think they are, strolling about like that? | Look at the mud on #topic.subject#.
b[priest] : Kindness to the stranger. It's written.
b : After the road? We all could use one. | A traveller. Let them stroll. | Muddy roads.
a : Some more than others. | Strolling's free, I suppose. | Muddy everything.

scene ev_pl_strong
when topic=player topic.known=no a.job=laborer|soldier|guard|smith|miner
a : I bet #topic.subject# could lift a cart. | Shoulders on #topic.subject#. I'd not like to quarrel. | Bet #topic.subject# could swing a hammer.
b : Ask them to help unload. | Nor me. | Hire them.
a : I might. | Wise. | If they're for hire.

scene ev_pl_hungry_look
when topic=player topic.known=no here.place=market|street
a : See #topic.subject# eyeing the bread stall? | I think #topic.subject# hasn't eaten today. | I saw #topic.subject# count their coins twice.
b[baker] : They can have the burnt end. No charge.
b[merchant] : I'll do a fair price. Even for strangers.
b : Poor thing. | Looks thin. | Short, maybe.
a : We've all been there. | Thin as a rake. | We've all been there.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Someone they know

scene ev_pk_back
when topic=player topic.known=yes
a : There's #topic.subject#, back again. | Look, it's #topic.subject#. | #topic.subject#'s around again, I see.
b[merchant] : Good. They pay on time. A rare thing.
b[child] : #topic.subject#! Do you think they'll show me the trick again?
b : Haven't seen them in a while. | Good. I like them. | So I see.
a : Busy, I suppose. | Easy to like. | Hard to miss.

scene ev_pk_well_thought
when topic=player topic.known=yes
a : #topic.subject# helped me fix my cart. Good sort. | #topic.subject# always says good morning. Nobody else does. | I trust #topic.subject#. Not many I do.
b[old] : Manners are rare. Keep hold of the ones who have them.
b : That's decent of them. | Nobody does. | That's saying something.
a : More than decent. | I noticed. | It is.

scene ev_pk_debt
when topic=player topic.known=yes a.role=merchant
a : #topic.subject# still owes me for last time. | #topic.subject# drives a hard bargain. | #topic.subject# bought half my stock. I could kiss them.
b : Remind them. | Respect, then. | Don't. Just smile.
a : Gently. They're good for it. | Grudging respect. | I'll smile all day.

scene ev_pk_gossip_about
when topic=player topic.known=yes
a : Did #topic.subject# tell you where they've been? | #topic.subject# came in with a fresh scar. | #topic.subject# looks tired today.
b[healer] : I'll take a look, if they'll let me.
b : Never says much. | Trouble on the road? | Long days, maybe.
a : Close as a clam, that one. | They didn't say. | We all have them.

scene ev_pk_friendly_wave
when topic=player topic.known=yes here.place=street|market|gate
a : Give #topic.subject# a wave. | Shall we ask #topic.subject# to supper? | #topic.subject#'s always in a hurry, isn't it?
b : There. Waved. | Why not. | Places to be.
a : They saw. | I'll ask. | Always.

scene ev_pk_tavern
when topic=player topic.known=yes here.place=tavern
a : #topic.subject# owes me a song from last time. | Save #topic.subject# a seat. | #topic.subject# drinks like a fish and never gets drunk.
b[innkeeper] : I'd be glad of a good customer tonight.
b : Make them sing. | Done. | Must be a gift.
a : Loud, too. | Good. | Or a hollow leg.

scene ev_pk_wary
when topic=player topic.known=yes
a : #topic.subject# again. I don't know about them. | Something about #topic.subject# bothers me. | #topic.subject# asks a lot of questions.
b[guard] : I've noted their comings and goings.
b : They've done nothing wrong. | You're too careful. | Curious, that's all.
a : Not that I've seen. | Better careful. | Maybe.

scene ev_pk_child_admires
when topic=player topic.known=yes a.stage=young|adolescent
a : I want to be like #topic.subject# when I'm grown. | #topic.subject# told me about the far mountains! | #topic.subject# is the bravest wolf I know.
b[old] : Grow up yourself first, then decide.
b : Do you, now? | Did they? | How do you know?
a : Yes! | They saw snow on the peaks in summer! | I just know.

scene ev_pk_old_approves
when topic=player topic.known=yes a.stage=old
a : #topic.subject# has good manners. Rare in the young. | #topic.subject# carried my basket yesterday. | #topic.subject# reminds me of my son.
b : They're a good one. | Kind of them. | Does he still write?
a : Raised right. | Wouldn't take a penny. | Not often.

scene ev_pk_priest
when topic=player topic.known=yes a.job=priest
a : I hope #topic.subject# comes to prayers this Restday. | #topic.subject# gave alms last time. Generous. | I pray for #topic.subject# on the road.
b : Maybe. | Generous indeed. | Kind of you.
a : The door's open. | The Bright One sees it. | Every traveller needs it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- More strangers, by who is looking

scene ev_pl_healer_notices
when topic=player topic.known=no a.job=healer
a : Did you see how #topic.subject# favours one leg? | I don't like the colour of the eyes on #topic.subject#. Fever, maybe. | I'd bet my herbs #topic.subject# hasn't slept in days.
b : I didn't notice. | You see sickness everywhere. | Neither have I.
a : A healer notices. | Because it's everywhere. | Then we're a pair.

scene ev_pl_innkeeper_sizes
when topic=player topic.known=no a.job=innkeeper
a : I'll have a room for #topic.subject# tonight, mark me. | Watch, #topic.subject# will ask for the stew. Travellers always do. | I can tell what #topic.subject# drinks from here. Dark ale.
b : You can't know that. | Everyone asks for the stew. | How?
a : Thirty years behind a counter. | Because it's good stew. | The way they lean.

scene ev_pl_guard_notes
when topic=player topic.known=no a.job=guard|soldier
a : Note it down: #topic.subject#, came in at noon. | Watch #topic.subject#. Paws near the purse, eyes on the stalls. | No weapon on #topic.subject# that I can see. Good.
b : Noted. | Watching. | Or one we can't see.
a : Good. | Don't let them see you watch. | That's the worry.

scene ev_pl_merchant_appraises
when topic=player topic.known=no a.role=merchant
a : Purse on #topic.subject# looks heavy. Hello, customer. | I'll bet #topic.subject# needs boots. Look at those soles. | Somebody tell #topic.subject# my prices are the best in #here.town#.
b : Don't fleece them. | They do look worn. | Tell them yourself.
a : Only a little. | Boots, and a new cloak. | I'm about to.

scene ev_pl_farmer_squint
when topic=player topic.known=no a.job=farmer|herder
a : Do you suppose #topic.subject# knows one end of a plough from the other? | Town paws on #topic.subject#. Soft. | Wonder if #topic.subject# wants work. I need hands at harvest.
b : Doubt it. | Soft as butter. | Ask them.
a : Nor do half the wolves here. | Soft paws, sore by evening. | I might.

scene ev_pl_priest_welcome
when topic=player topic.known=no a.job=priest
a : We should welcome #topic.subject#. The road is lonely. | I wonder if #topic.subject# has found a bed tonight. | The Bright One sends us strangers to test our kindness.
b : Go on, then. | The chapel has cots. | And our patience.
a : I will, in a moment. | I'll tell them. | That too.

scene ev_pl_scholar_curious
when topic=player topic.known=no a.job=scholar
a : I'd give a lot to hear where #topic.subject# has been. | The accent on #topic.subject#. Western, I'd wager. | Do you think #topic.subject# reads?
b : Ask them. | You can tell from an accent? | Doubt it.
a : I'd lose my nerve. | Vowels like river stones. Western. | Everyone should.

scene ev_pl_noble_dismiss
when topic=player topic.known=no a.job=noble
a : Must we have every vagabond in the square? Like #topic.subject#? | Have someone see what #topic.subject# wants. | Ugh, #topic.subject# is staring at me.
b : It's a public square. | I'll ask. | They stare at everyone.
a : More's the pity. | Discreetly. | Not everyone is worth it.

scene ev_pl_beggar_hopes
when topic=player topic.known=no a.job=beggar
a : Maybe #topic.subject# has a coin to spare. | I've seen kinder faces than the one on #topic.subject#. | Bet #topic.subject# gives. They've the look.
b : Ask nicely. | And crueler ones. | Hope so.
a : I always ask nicely. | Plenty crueler. | Here goes.

scene ev_pl_carter_road_news
when topic=player topic.known=no a.job=carter
a : Came by the east road, I'd wager. Ask #topic.subject# if it's clear. | I passed #topic.subject# on the road yesterday. Walks fast. | Mud on #topic.subject# means the ford's still up.
b : Ask them yourself. | Walks fast? On foot? | Is it?
a : I will, once they've rested. | Faster than my mule. | Up to the axles, I'd say.

scene ev_pl_old_memory
when topic=player topic.known=no a.stage=old
a : I used to walk the roads like #topic.subject#, once. | Watching #topic.subject# makes me feel old. | Young ones on the road. Like #topic.subject#. Brave or foolish.
b : Did you? | You are old. | Both, usually.
a : Every road from here to the sea. | Thank you, pup. | Both.

scene ev_pl_two_kids
when topic=player topic.known=no a.stage=young|adolescent b.stage=young|adolescent
a : Bet you can't go and talk to #topic.subject#. | I dare you to sniff #topic.subject#. | Do you think #topic.subject# has treasure?
b : Bet I can! | No! You do it! | A whole bag of it!
a : Go on, then! | Coward! | Let's follow them!

scene ev_pl_rain_stranger
when topic=player topic.known=no here.weather=rain|storm|snow
a : Poor #topic.subject#, out in this weather. | Look at #topic.subject#, soaked to the bone. | Somebody give #topic.subject# a roof.
b : Their choice. | Wet as a fish. | The inn has room.
a : Nobody chooses this. | Drowned rat. | I'll point the way.

scene ev_pl_festival_stranger
when topic=player topic.known=no here.day=festival
a : Do you think #topic.subject# came for the festival? | Festival brings all sorts. Look at #topic.subject#. | Bet #topic.subject# has never seen a festival like ours.
b : Everyone comes for the festival. | All sorts and their cousins. | Then they're in for a treat.
a : Good for trade. | And their cousins' cousins. | A treat and a sore head.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- More travellers known by name

scene ev_pk_long_absence
when topic=player topic.known=yes
a : I thought #topic.subject# had gone for good. | #topic.subject# was away so long I'd forgotten their voice. | Where has #topic.subject# been all this time?
b : Seems not. | Ask them to sing. | Roads, I suppose.
a : Glad to be wrong. | Ha. Maybe. | Long roads.

scene ev_pk_helped
when topic=player topic.known=yes
a : #topic.subject# found my lost pup last spring. | #topic.subject# stood up to that drunk for me. | I owe #topic.subject# more than a drink.
b : I remember. | Brave. | Then buy two.
a : I'll never forget it. | Braver than I was. | Three, then.

scene ev_pk_rumour
when topic=player topic.known=yes
a : People say #topic.subject# has been in trouble. | I heard #topic.subject# is gifted. Is it true? | They say #topic.subject# came from far across the mountains.
b[priest] : Rumour is the Dark One's favourite tool. Hold your tongue.
b : People say lots of things. | Who knows. | Maybe.
a : They do. | Who knows. | Far from here, anyway.

scene ev_pk_guard
when topic=player topic.known=yes a.job=guard|soldier
a : #topic.subject# is no trouble. Leave them be. | #topic.subject# again. Keep half an eye. | I've seen #topic.subject# draw a blade. Quick.
b : Understood. | Half an eye. | Glad they're not against us.
a : Good. | And the other half on the crowd. | So am I.

scene ev_pk_spouses
when topic=player topic.known=yes pair.band=spouses
a : #topic.subject# is back, love. | Shall we have #topic.subject# round for supper? | You were sweet on #topic.subject# once, weren't you?
b : Is that so? | If you're cooking. | Before I met you.
a : By the well. | I'll cook. | Hmm.

scene ev_pk_rivals
when topic=player topic.known=yes pair.band=rivals
a : I suppose you're friends with #topic.subject# too. | #topic.subject# likes me better than you. | #topic.subject# told me what you said about them.
b : Better than with you. | Dream on. | Liar.
a : Hm. | I don't dream. | Ask them, then.

scene ev_pk_tavern_story
when topic=player topic.known=yes here.place=tavern here.time=dusk|night
a : Get #topic.subject# to tell the story about the bandits. | #topic.subject# was in here last night till the lamps went out. | Last time #topic.subject# drank, they danced on a table.
b[innkeeper] : And broke a leg off it. Which I've not forgotten.
b : I've heard it. It grows each time. | They have a gift for staying. | I'd pay to see that again.
a : Better every time. | A gift, yes. | So would I.

scene ev_pk_merchant_regular
when topic=player topic.known=yes here.place=market
a : #topic.subject# will want the usual. | Here comes #topic.subject#. Put on a smile. | #topic.subject# always haggles. Every time.
b : What's the usual? | I'm always smiling. | So do you.
a : Two loaves and a bit of cheese. | You're baring teeth. | And I enjoy it.

scene ev_pk_child_follows
when topic=player topic.known=yes a.stage=young
a : Can I go play with #topic.subject#? | #topic.subject# gave me a sweet once! | Is #topic.subject# in the watch?
b[old] : Don't pester our guests, pup.
b : Ask nicely. | Did they? | I don't think so.
a : Please? | A sticky one! | They should be.
